    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d632">

                <pb facs="0623" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg525"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July 26,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1319.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have to report that at the request of Lady Randolph Churchill I notified Count
                    Bülow informally that the American hospital ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maine</hi> had sailed for Chinese waters on the 12th instant, and that if
                    any wounded German soldiers or sailors require aid they will be welcome to her
                    and every assistance possible will be given them.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
